## Tradeoffs

| Benefit | Cost |
|---|---|
| Persistent project guidance | Staleness risk |
| Explicit scope boundaries | Ongoing ownership |
| Shared commands and standards | Context-token overhead |

## Anti-Patterns

- Embedding credentials, tokens, or sensitive customer data.
- Requiring exposed private chain-of-thought.
- Using this file as an authorization mechanism.
- Keeping obsolete commands or architecture.

## Enterprise Considerations

Assign an owner, classify the file, review changes through normal code ownership, and keep policy enforcement in identity, access-control, CI, and deployment systems.

